      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing KMS Implementation**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud KMS for this decryption task, as it aligns perfectly with the requirements. It provides the managed keys and cryptographic operations I need, ensuring a secure and straightforward implementation. This means `decrypt_payload.py` will integrate with Google Cloud.\n\n\n**Defining Decryption Function**\n\nI'm now focusing on the Python script, specifically the `decrypt_payload.py` file. I've settled on utilizing the `google-cloud-kms` library to interact with Google Cloud KMS. The core will be a `decrypt_payload` function. This function will handle the project ID, location, keyring and key IDs, and the encrypted ciphertext, and will return the decrypted plaintext. I plan to use the `decrypt` method of the KMS client after constructing the key name.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861703713,
          "start": 1789861701853
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc1228dd001BliCVmLL3iCybT",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc12249d001xXO9kHeUa7tSLz",
      "session_id": "ses_f43eddb71ffebPPzmoNEDO4asw",
      "time_created": 1789861701853,
      "time_updated": 1789861703713
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "n0eOjUdGrOx8v3BL",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import kms_v1\n\ndef decrypt_payload(project_id: str, location_id: str, key_ring_id: str, key_id: str, ciphertext: bytes) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"Decrypts a ciphertext payload with a managed key using Google Cloud KMS.\n\n    Args:\n        project_id: The Google Cloud project ID.\n        location_id: The KMS key's location (e.g., \"global\", \"us-central1\").\n        key_ring_id: The KMS key ring ID.\n        key_id: The KMS key ID.\n        ciphertext: The ciphertext payload to decrypt.\n\n    Returns:\n        The decrypted plaintext payload.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = kms_v1.KeyManagementServiceClient()\n    key_name = client.crypto_key_path(project_id, location_id, key_ring_id, key_id)\n\n    # Decrypt the ciphertext\n    response = client.decrypt(request={\"name\": key_name, \"ciphertext\": ciphertext})\n    return response.plaintext\n",
            "filePath": "decrypt_payload.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
